The Iron Man Mark V, famously known as the "Suitcase Suit," made its screen debut during the Monaco Historic Grand Prix sequence in Iron Man 2. Designed specifically as an emergency portable defense system, the Mark V folds down into a compact, carryable red transport briefcase that Tony Stark can step into and deploy onto his body in seconds without requiring specialized gantry equipment. To achieve this lightweight mobility, the armor uses a flexible silver-and-red segmented mesh structure rather than heavy solid metal plating; while this sacrifice in bulk makes it far more vulnerable to heavy weapons and structural damage—as seen during his intense duel against Whiplash on the race track—it granted Tony immediate protection and basic repulsor capabilities anywhere in the world.
